#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use IBM Cloud Resource Controller API for instance management {#use-ibm-cloud-resource-controller-api-for-instance-management}"
msgstr "Utiliser l'API IBM Cloud Resource Controller pour la gestion des instances {#use-ibm-cloud-resource-controller-api-for-instance-management}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use the IBM Cloud&reg; Resource Controller REST API to programmatically get, create, and update [instances](/guides/instances). \n"
msgstr "Tu peux utiliser l'API REST IBM Cloud&reg; Resource Controller pour obtenir, créer et mettre à jour des [instances](/guides/instances) de manière programmatique. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All Resource Controller endpoints require that you authenticate by passing a header called `Authorization` with the bearer token. Refer to the [REST API setup guide](/guides/cloud-setup-rest-api).\n"
msgstr "Tous les points de terminaison du Resource Controller exigent que tu t'authentifies en transmettant un en-tête appelé `Authorization` avec le jeton porteur. Consulte le [guide de configuration de l'API REST](/guides/cloud-setup-rest-api).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get an instance {#get-an-instance}"
msgstr "Obtenir une instance {#get-an-instance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the [`GET /v2/resource_instances/{crn}`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#get-resource-instance) endpoint to get information about a particular instance. The [CRN](/guides/instances) must be URL-encoded in the path.\n"
msgstr "Utilise le point de terminaison [`GET /v2/resource_instances/{crn}`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#get-resource-instance) pour obtenir des informations sur une instance particulière. Le [CRN](/guides/instances) doit être encodé en URL dans le chemin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to the standard Resource Controller fields, the response includes quantum-specific fields in both `parameters` and `extensions`. `extensions` stores the instance's normalized metadata, whereas `parameters` only stores the most recent request to modify the instance. Therefore, you should read from `extensions` rather than `parameters`.\n"
msgstr "En plus des champs standard du Resource Controller, la réponse inclut des champs spécifiques à quantum à la fois dans `parameters` et dans `extensions`. `extensions` stocke les métadonnées normalisées de l'instance, tandis que `parameters` ne stocke que la demande de modification la plus récente de l'instance. Par conséquent, tu devrais lire à partir de `extensions` plutôt que de `parameters`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `extensions` object includes these fields:\n"
msgstr "L'objet `extensions` inclut ces champs :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`instance_limit_seconds` — Integer, or `null`. The usage time limit for the instance. See [Set instance allocation limits](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"
msgstr "`instance_limit_seconds` — Entier, ou `null`. La limite de temps d'utilisation pour l'instance. Voir [Définir les limites d'allocation d'instance](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage_allocation_seconds` — Integer, or `null`. The time allocated to this instance, used by the [fair-share scheduler](/guides/fair-share-scheduler) to determine queue priority. See [Set instance allocation limits](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"
msgstr "`usage_allocation_seconds` — Entier, ou `null`. Le temps alloué à cette instance, utilisé par l'[ordonnanceur à partage équitable](/guides/fair-share-scheduler) pour déterminer la priorité dans la file d'attente. Voir [Définir les limites d'allocation d'instance](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`backends` — Array of strings. The allowlist of backend names available to this instance. `[\"ANY\"]` means all backends on the plan are available (the default). `[]` means no backends are available.\n"
msgstr "`backends` — Tableau de chaînes. La liste d'autorisation des noms de backends disponibles pour cette instance. `[\"ANY\"]` signifie que tous les backends du plan sont disponibles (valeur par défaut). `[]` signifie qu'aucun backend n'est disponible.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"The backends field may be outdated\">\n"
"  The `backends` field in the `extensions` object may be outdated. This can happen when IBM Quantum Support changes your account in a way that impacts instances. For example, when a backend is removed from an account, it will update the `backends` for the instance, but that change is currently not yet reflected in the Resource Controller API.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Le champ backends peut être obsolète\">\n"
"  Le champ `backends` de l'objet `extensions` peut être obsolète. Cela peut se produire lorsque le support IBM Quantum modifie ton compte d'une manière qui affecte les instances. Par exemple, lorsqu'un backend est retiré d'un compte, cela met à jour les `backends` de l'instance, mais ce changement n'est actuellement pas encore reflété dans l'API Resource Controller.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Instead, the current workaround is to use the [IBM Quantum Compute Service REST API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest) with the [`GET /v1/backends`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest/tags/backends#tags__backends__operations__list_backends) endpoint. (Make sure that you set the `Service-CRN` header to your instance's CRN.)\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  À la place, la solution de contournement actuelle consiste à utiliser l'[API REST IBM Quantum Compute Service](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest) avec le point de terminaison [`GET /v1/backends`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest/tags/backends#tags__backends__operations__list_backends). (Assure-toi de définir l'en-tête `Service-CRN` sur le CRN de ton instance.)\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"    The CRN must be URL-encoded in the path. Replace each `:` with `%3A` and each `/` with `%2F`. For example, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` becomes `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"    Le CRN doit être encodé en URL dans le chemin. Remplace chaque `:` par `%3A` et chaque `/` par `%2F`. Par exemple, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` devient `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    curl \\\n"
"      --request GET \\\n"
"      --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"      --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"Python\">\n"
msgstr "  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"Python\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import urllib.parse\n"
"    import requests\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"
"    # We use urllib.parse.quote to URL-encode the CRN.\n"
"    url = (\n"
"        \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"        + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
"    )\n"
msgstr ""
"    crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"
"    # Nous utilisons urllib.parse.quote pour encoder le CRN en URL.\n"
"    url = (\n"
"        \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"        + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
"    )\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    resp = requests.get(\n"
"        url,\n"
"        headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"},\n"
"        timeout=30,\n"
"    )\n"
"    resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    print(resp.json())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    resp = requests.get(\n"
"        url,\n"
"        headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"},\n"
"        timeout=30,\n"
"    )\n"
"    resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    print(resp.json())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get a list of all instances {#get-a-list-of-all-instances}"
msgstr "Obtenir une liste de toutes les instances {#get-a-list-of-all-instances}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the [`GET /v2/resource_instances`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#list-resource-instances) endpoint to get a list of all your instances. Set the `resource_id` query parameter to `b6049020-80f4-11eb-a0f7-e35ec9b4054f` to filter to IBM Quantum&reg; instances.\n"
