#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update an instance {#update-an-instance}"
msgstr "Mettre à jour une instance {#update-an-instance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the [`PATCH /v2/resource_instances/{crn}`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#update-resource-instance) endpoint to update the limit, allocation, and permitted backends for an instance. The [CRN](/guides/instances) must be URL-encoded in the path.\n"
msgstr "Utilise le point de terminaison [`PATCH /v2/resource_instances/{crn}`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#update-resource-instance) pour mettre à jour la limite, l'allocation et les backends autorisés pour une instance. Le [CRN](/guides/instances) doit être encodé en URL dans le chemin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass a `parameters` JSON object in the request body with the fields you want to change, along with the header `\"Content-Type: application/json\"`. Omitted fields are left unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Transmets un objet JSON `parameters` dans le corps de la requête avec les champs que tu souhaites modifier, ainsi que l'en-tête `\"Content-Type: application/json\"`. Les champs omis restent inchangés.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage_allocation_seconds` — Integer, or `null`. The time allocated to this instance, used by the [fair-share scheduler](/guides/fair-share-scheduler) to determine queue priority. See [Set instance allocation limits](/guides/allocation-limits). Not applicable to Pay-As-You-Go instances.\n"
msgstr "`usage_allocation_seconds` — Entier, ou `null`. Le temps alloué à cette instance, utilisé par l'[ordonnanceur à partage équitable](/guides/fair-share-scheduler) pour déterminer la priorité dans la file d'attente. Voir [Définir les limites d'allocation d'instance](/guides/allocation-limits). Ne s'applique pas aux instances Pay-As-You-Go.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`backends` — Array of strings. The allowlist of backend names available to this instance. `[\"ANY\"]` means all backends on the plan are available. `[]` means no backends are available.\n"
msgstr "`backends` — Tableau de chaînes. La liste d'autorisation des noms de backends disponibles pour cette instance. `[\"ANY\"]` signifie que tous les backends du plan sont disponibles. `[]` signifie qu'aucun backend n'est disponible.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Always include a unique timestamp\">\n"
"  The API silently ignores the request if `parameters` is identical to the previous request. In the `parameters` object, always include a `timestamp` field set to the current time so each request is treated as unique.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Inclus toujours un horodatage unique\">\n"
"  L'API ignore silencieusement la requête si `parameters` est identique à la requête précédente. Dans l'objet `parameters`, inclus toujours un champ `timestamp` défini sur l'heure actuelle afin que chaque requête soit traitée comme unique.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The endpoint's response is similar to [getting an instance](#get-an-instance), including how it handles the `extensions` object.\n"
msgstr "La réponse du point de terminaison est similaire à celle de [l'obtention d'une instance](#get-an-instance), y compris la façon dont elle gère l'objet `extensions`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    curl \\\n"
"    --request PATCH \\\n"
"    --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"    --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>' \\\n"
"    --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"    --data \"{\n"
"        \\\"parameters\\\": {\n"
"            \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"$(date -u +\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\\\",\n"
"            \\\"usage_allocation_seconds\\\": 220\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\"\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import urllib.parse\n"
"    import datetime\n"
"    import requests\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    timestamp = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n"
"    body = {\n"
"        \"parameters\": {\n"
"            \"timestamp\": timestamp,\n"
"            \"usage_allocation_seconds\": 220,\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""
"    timestamp = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n"
"    body = {\n"
"        \"parameters\": {\n"
"            \"timestamp\": timestamp,\n"
"            \"usage_allocation_seconds\": 220,\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    resp = requests.patch(\n"
"        url,\n"
"        headers={\n"
"            \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\",\n"
"            \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n"
"        },\n"
"        json=body,\n"
"        timeout=30,\n"
"    )\n"
"    resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    print(resp.json())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    resp = requests.patch(\n"
"        url,\n"
"        headers={\n"
"            \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\",\n"
"            \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n"
"        },\n"
"        json=body,\n"
"        timeout=30,\n"
"    )\n"
"    resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    print(resp.json())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create a new instance {#create-a-new-instance}"
msgstr "Créer une nouvelle instance {#create-a-new-instance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the [`POST /v2/resource_instances`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#create-resource-instance) endpoint to create (provision) a new instance. Pass a JSON body with the header `\"Content-Type: application/json\"`.\n"
msgstr "Utilise le point de terminaison [`POST /v2/resource_instances`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#create-resource-instance) pour créer (provisionner) une nouvelle instance. Transmets un corps JSON avec l'en-tête `\"Content-Type: application/json\"`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Required fields:\n"
msgstr "Champs obligatoires :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`name` — A human-readable name for the instance.\n"
msgstr "`name` — Un nom lisible par un humain pour l'instance.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`target` — The region, such as `us-east` or `eu-de`.\n"
msgstr "`target` — La région, par exemple `us-east` ou `eu-de`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`resource_plan_id` — The plan for this instance. See the [plan ID table](#get-a-list-of-all-instances).\n"
msgstr "`resource_plan_id` — Le plan pour cette instance. Voir le [tableau des ID de plan](#get-a-list-of-all-instances).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`resource_group` — The [resource group](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-rgs) to use.\n"
msgstr "`resource_group` — Le [groupe de ressources](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-rgs) à utiliser.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also include a `parameters` object to set quantum-specific values:\n"
msgstr "Tu peux également inclure un objet `parameters` pour définir des valeurs spécifiques à quantum :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    curl \\\n"
"      --request POST \\\n"
"      --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances' \\\n"
"      --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>' \\\n"
"      --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"      --data '{\n"
"          \"name\": \"my-new-instance\",\n"
"          \"target\": \"us-east\",\n"
"          \"resource_plan_id\": \"7f666d17-7893-47d8-bf9d-2b2389fc4dfc\",\n"
"          \"resource_group\": \"<YOUR_RESOURCE_GROUP_ID>\",\n"
"          \"parameters\": {\n"
"              \"instance_limit_seconds\": 300,\n"
"              \"usage_allocation_seconds\": 220\n"
"          }\n"
"      }'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    body = {\n"
"        \"name\": \"my-new-instance\",\n"
"        \"target\": \"us-east\",\n"
"        \"resource_plan_id\": \"7f666d17-7893-47d8-bf9d-2b2389fc4dfc\",\n"
"        \"resource_group\": \"<YOUR_RESOURCE_GROUP_ID>\",\n"
"        \"parameters\": {\n"
"            \"instance_limit_seconds\": 300,\n"
"            \"usage_allocation_seconds\": 220,\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""
"    body = {\n"
"        \"name\": \"my-new-instance\",\n"
"        \"target\": \"us-east\",\n"
"        \"resource_plan_id\": \"7f666d17-7893-47d8-bf9d-2b2389fc4dfc\",\n"
"        \"resource_group\": \"<YOUR_RESOURCE_GROUP_ID>\",\n"
"        \"parameters\": {\n"
"            \"instance_limit_seconds\": 300,\n"
"            \"usage_allocation_seconds\": 220,\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    resp = requests.post(\n"
"        \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances\",\n"
"        headers={\n"
"            \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\",\n"
"            \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n"
"        },\n"
"        json=body,\n"
"        timeout=30,\n"
"    )\n"
"    resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    print(resp.json())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    resp = requests.post(\n"
"        \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances\",\n"
"        headers={\n"
"            \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\",\n"
"            \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n"
"        },\n"
"        json=body,\n"
"        timeout=30,\n"
"    )\n"
"    resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    print(resp.json())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"functions-api\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure Qiskit Functions access on an instance {#configure-qiskit-functions-access-on-an-instance}"
msgstr "Configurer l'accès aux Qiskit Functions sur une instance {#configure-qiskit-functions-access-on-an-instance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use these instructions to configure Qiskit Functions access on an existing IBM Quantum Compute Service instance by using the IBM Cloud Resource Controller API.  Follow the instructions in order, as the commands build on each other.  For example, variables such as the token and URL are set in one step and reused in later steps. \n"
msgstr "Utilise ces instructions pour configurer l'accès aux Qiskit Functions sur une instance IBM Quantum Compute Service existante à l'aide de l'API IBM Cloud Resource Controller.  Suis les instructions dans l'ordre, car les commandes s'appuient les unes sur les autres.  Par exemple, des variables telles que le jeton et l'URL sont définies à une étape et réutilisées dans les étapes suivantes. \n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prerequisites {#prerequisites}"
msgstr "Prérequis {#prerequisites}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An IBM Cloud API key (also called a token).  If necessary, create your API key on the [dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com). \n"
msgstr "Une clé API IBM Cloud (aussi appelée jeton).  Si nécessaire, crée ta clé API sur le [tableau de bord](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com). \n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The CRN of the instance you want to configure.  The instance's CRN is listed on your [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances) page.\n"
msgstr "Le CRN de l'instance que tu souhaites configurer.  Le CRN de l'instance est répertorié sur ta page [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Get a bearer token {#step-1-get-a-bearer-token}"
msgstr "Étape 1 : Obtenir un jeton porteur {#step-1-get-a-bearer-token}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exchange your API key for a bearer token. You will pass this token in the authorization header of all resource controller requests. Run the following code to generate a bearer token:\n"
msgstr "Échange ta clé API contre un jeton porteur. Tu transmettras ce jeton dans l'en-tête d'autorisation de toutes les requêtes du Resource Controller. Exécute le code suivant pour générer un jeton porteur :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request POST \\\n"
"  --url 'https://iam.cloud.ibm.com/identity/token' \\\n"
"  --header 'Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded' \\\n"
"  --data 'apikey=<YOUR_API_KEY>&grant_type=urn%3Aibm%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Aapikey'\n"
"  --silent | jq .\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"import requests\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "api_key = \"<YOUR_API_KEY>\"\n"
msgstr "api_key = \"<YOUR_API_KEY>\"\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.post(\n"
"    \"https://iam.cloud.ibm.com/identity/token\",\n"
"    headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\"},\n"
"    params={\n"
"        \"apikey\": api_key,\n"
"        \"grant_type\": \"urn:ibm:params:oauth:grant-type:apikey\",\n"
"    },\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"token = resp.json()[\"access_token\"]\n"
"print(token) \n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.post(\n"
"    \"https://iam.cloud.ibm.com/identity/token\",\n"
"    headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\"},\n"
"    params={\n"
"        \"apikey\": api_key,\n"
"        \"grant_type\": \"urn:ibm:params:oauth:grant-type:apikey\",\n"
"    },\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"token = resp.json()[\"access_token\"]\n"
"print(token) \n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The response includes an `access_token` field, which is your bearer token. Copy this value.\n"
msgstr "La réponse inclut un champ `access_token`, qui est ton jeton porteur. Copie cette valeur.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Verify access {#step-2-verify-access}"
msgstr "Étape 2 : Vérifier l'accès {#step-2-verify-access}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before making any changes, confirm that your token works and inspect the current instance configuration.\n"
msgstr "Avant d'apporter des modifications, confirme que ton jeton fonctionne et vérifie la configuration actuelle de l'instance.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important\">\n"
"The CRN must be manually URL-encoded in the path. Replace each `:` with `%3A` and each `/` with `%2F`. For example, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` becomes `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important\">\n"
"Le CRN doit être encodé manuellement en URL dans le chemin. Remplace chaque `:` par `%3A` et chaque `/` par `%2F`. Par exemple, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` devient `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request GET \\\n"
"  --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"import urllib.parse\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"
msgstr "crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "The CRN will be URL-encoded into the path."
msgstr "Le CRN sera encodé en URL dans le chemin."

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"instance_url = (\n"
"    \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"    + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
")\n"
"headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}\n"
msgstr ""
"instance_url = (\n"
"    \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"    + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
")\n"
"headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.get(instance_url, headers=headers, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.get(instance_url, headers=headers, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `200 OK` response confirms that your token is valid. The current instance configuration is in the extensions field of the response. Use this instead of parameters, which might be stale.\n"
msgstr "Une réponse `200 OK` confirme que ton jeton est valide. La configuration actuelle de l'instance se trouve dans le champ extensions de la réponse. Utilise celui-ci plutôt que parameters, qui pourrait être obsolète.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"step-3\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Look up the account-level functions configuration {#step-3-look-up-the-account-level-functions-configuration}"
msgstr "Étape 3 : Rechercher la configuration des fonctions au niveau du compte {#step-3-look-up-the-account-level-functions-configuration}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An instance can only be granted access to what the account is entitled to. Before configuring the instance, look up the account's configuration so you know which functions, business models, and permissions are available to grant. This is the source of truth for the values you will send in Step 4.\n"
msgstr "Une instance ne peut se voir accorder l'accès qu'à ce à quoi le compte a droit. Avant de configurer l'instance, recherche la configuration du compte afin de connaître les fonctions, modèles économiques et autorisations disponibles à accorder. C'est la source de vérité pour les valeurs que tu enverras à l'étape 4.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Call `GET /accounts/{id}` on the Qiskit Runtime API with your API key. The `{id}` is your account ID without the `a/` prefix.  You can find it from the instance CRN (`crn:v1:bluemix:public:quantum-computing:...:a/<ACCOUNT_ID>:...`).\n"
msgstr "Appelle `GET /accounts/{id}` sur l'API Qiskit Runtime avec ta clé API. `{id}` est ton ID de compte sans le préfixe `a/`.  Tu peux le trouver à partir du CRN de l'instance (`crn:v1:bluemix:public:quantum-computing:...:a/<ACCOUNT_ID>:...`).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request GET \\\n"
"  --url 'https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/accounts/<ACCOUNT_ID>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: apikey <YOUR_API_KEY>'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"account_id = \"<ACCOUNT_ID>\"  # from the CRN: crn:...:a/<ACCOUNT_ID>:...\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.get(\n"
"    f\"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/accounts/{account_id}\",\n"
"    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"apikey {api_key}\"},\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"for plan in resp.json()[\"plans\"]:\n"
"    print(plan[\"plan_id\"], plan.get(\"functions\"), plan.get(\"custom_functions\"))\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.get(\n"
"    f\"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/accounts/{account_id}\",\n"
"    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"apikey {api_key}\"},\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"for plan in resp.json()[\"plans\"]:\n"
"    print(plan[\"plan_id\"], plan.get(\"functions\"), plan.get(\"custom_functions\"))\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each plan in the response includes a functions array and, if configured, a `custom_functions` object. These list the exact name, provider, business model, and permissions values you can grant to an instance under that plan.\n"
msgstr "Chaque plan de la réponse inclut un tableau functions et, si configuré, un objet `custom_functions`. Ceux-ci répertorient le nom exact, le fournisseur, le modèle économique et les valeurs d'autorisations que tu peux accorder à une instance dans le cadre de ce plan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"`GET /accounts/{id}` shows what is available to grant at the account level. `GET /functions` (see [Verify the result](#verify-result)) shows what a specific instance has already been granted. Use the **account** endpoint to discover valid values, and the **functions** endpoint to confirm the result.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Configure functions access {#step-4-configure-functions-access}"
msgstr "Étape 4 : Configurer l'accès aux fonctions {#step-4-configure-functions-access}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the instance to grant access to Catalog Functions and Custom Functions.\n"
msgstr "Mets à jour l'instance pour accorder l'accès aux Catalog Functions et Custom Functions.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important notes\">\n"
"- The `name`, `provider`, and `business_model` values in functions must exactly match entries configured at the account level (see the [previous step](#step-3)). Permissions must be a non-empty subset of the account's permissions for that function. Similarly, `custom_functions.permissions` must be a non-empty subset of the account's `custom_functions` permissions.\n"
"- Include a timestamp in parameters on every PATCH. The Resource Controller deduplicates PATCH requests by comparing incoming parameters to the last value it stored. If they match, the request is silently dropped with `200 OK` without reaching the service. Include a changing timestamp value to prevent this.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Remarques importantes\">\n"
"- Les valeurs `name`, `provider` et `business_model` dans functions doivent correspondre exactement aux entrées configurées au niveau du compte (voir l'[étape précédente](#step-3)). Les autorisations doivent être un sous-ensemble non vide des autorisations du compte pour cette fonction. De même, `custom_functions.permissions` doit être un sous-ensemble non vide des autorisations `custom_functions` du compte.\n"
"- Inclus un horodatage dans parameters à chaque PATCH. Le Resource Controller déduplique les requêtes PATCH en comparant les parameters entrants à la dernière valeur qu'il a stockée. S'ils correspondent, la requête est abandonnée silencieusement avec `200 OK` sans atteindre le service. Inclus une valeur d'horodatage changeante pour éviter cela.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request PATCH \\\n"
"  --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"  --data '{\n"
"    \"parameters\": {\n"
"      \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-30T00:00:00Z\",\n"
"      \"functions\": [\n"
"        {\n"
"          \"name\": \"<FUNCTION_NAME>\",\n"
"          \"provider\": \"<PROVIDER>\",\n"
"          \"business_model\": \"<BUSINESS_MODEL>\",\n"
"          \"permissions\": [\n"
"            \"function.read\",\n"
"            \"function.run\",\n"
"            \"function-files.read\",\n"
"            \"function-files.write\"\n"
"          ]\n"
"        }\n"
"      ],\n"
"      \"custom_functions\": {\n"
"        \"permissions\": [\n"
"          \"function-custom.write\",\n"
"          \"function-custom.run\"\n"
"        ]\n"
"      }\n"
"    }\n"
"  }'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"from datetime import datetime, timezone\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "A changing timestamp keeps the Resource Controller from de-duplicating the request."
msgstr "Un horodatage changeant empêche le Resource Controller de dédupliquer la requête."

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n"
"timestamp = _now.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.\") + f\"{_now.microsecond:06d}000Z\"\n"
msgstr ""
"_now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n"
"timestamp = _now.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.\") + f\"{_now.microsecond:06d}000Z\"\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"body = {\n"
"    \"parameters\": {\n"
"        \"timestamp\": timestamp,\n"
"        \"functions\": [\n"
"            {\n"
"                \"name\": \"<FUNCTION_NAME>\",\n"
"                \"provider\": \"<PROVIDER>\",\n"
"                \"business_model\": \"<BUSINESS_MODEL>\",\n"
"                \"permissions\": [\n"
"                    \"function.read\",\n"
"                    \"function.run\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.read\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.write\",\n"
"                ],\n"
"            }\n"
"        ],\n"
"        \"custom_functions\": {\n"
"            \"permissions\": [\"function-custom.write\", \"function-custom.run\"],\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"body = {\n"
"    \"parameters\": {\n"
"        \"timestamp\": timestamp,\n"
"        \"functions\": [\n"
"            {\n"
"                \"name\": \"<FUNCTION_NAME>\",\n"
"                \"provider\": \"<PROVIDER>\",\n"
"                \"business_model\": \"<BUSINESS_MODEL>\",\n"
"                \"permissions\": [\n"
"                    \"function.read\",\n"
"                    \"function.run\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.read\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.write\",\n"
"                ],\n"
"            }\n"
"        ],\n"
"        \"custom_functions\": {\n"
"            \"permissions\": [\"function-custom.write\", \"function-custom.run\"],\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `200 OK` response indicates success. The updated configuration appears in the extensions field of the response.\n"
msgstr "Une réponse `200 OK` indique le succès. La configuration mise à jour apparaît dans le champ extensions de la réponse.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove functions access {#remove-functions-access}"
msgstr "Supprimer l'accès aux fonctions {#remove-functions-access}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Catalog Functions {#catalog-functions}"
msgstr "Catalog Functions {#catalog-functions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To remove Catalog Functions from an instance, send a PATCH with `\"functions\": null`:\n"
msgstr "Pour supprimer les Catalog Functions d'une instance, envoie un PATCH avec `\"functions\": null` :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"--data '{\n"
"  \"parameters\": {\n"
"    \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-30T00:00:01Z\",\n"
"    \"functions\": null\n"
"  }\n"
"}'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"body = {\"parameters\": {\"timestamp\": timestamp, \"functions\": None}}\n"
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `\"functions\": []` (an empty array) equivalently clears Catalog Functions. `null` is the canonical form.\n"
msgstr "Définir `\"functions\": []` (un tableau vide) efface également les Catalog Functions de manière équivalente. `null` est la forme canonique.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom Functions {#custom-functions}"
msgstr "Custom Functions {#custom-functions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To remove Custom Functions from an instance, send a PATCH with `\"custom_functions\": null`:\n"
msgstr "Pour supprimer les Custom Functions d'une instance, envoie un PATCH avec `\"custom_functions\": null` :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"--data '{\n"
"  \"parameters\": {\n"
"    \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-30T00:00:02Z\",\n"
"    \"custom_functions\": null\n"
"  }\n"
"}'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"body = {\"parameters\": {\"timestamp\": timestamp, \"custom_functions\": None}}\n"
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `\"custom_functions\": {\"permissions\": []}` equivalently clears custom functions. `null` is the canonical form.\n"
msgstr "Définir `\"custom_functions\": {\"permissions\": []}` efface également les fonctions personnalisées de manière équivalente. `null` est la forme canonique.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-result\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verify the result {#verify-the-result}"
msgstr "Vérifier le résultat {#verify-the-result}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To confirm that the instance has the correct Qiskit Functions configuration, use `GET /functions` from the Qiskit Runtime API instead of the Resource Controller. The Resource Controller's stored state might be stale if account-level changes updated the instance outside of the Resource Controller.\n"
msgstr "Pour confirmer que l'instance dispose de la configuration Qiskit Functions correcte, utilise `GET /functions` de l'API Qiskit Runtime plutôt que le Resource Controller. L'état stocké du Resource Controller peut être obsolète si des modifications au niveau du compte ont mis à jour l'instance en dehors du Resource Controller.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request GET \\\n"
"  --url 'https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/functions' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: apikey <YOUR_API_KEY>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Service-CRN: <YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    ```python\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Service-CRN header takes the raw CRN, not the URL-encoded form."
msgstr "L'en-tête Service-CRN utilise le CRN brut, et non la forme encodée en URL."

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.get(\n"
"    \"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/functions\",\n"
"    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"apikey {api_key}\", \"Service-CRN\": crn},\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.get(\n"
"    \"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/functions\",\n"
"    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"apikey {api_key}\", \"Service-CRN\": crn},\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
